      <Comment>Phosphatidylethanolamines are a class of |FRAME: Phosphoglycerides phosphoglycerolipids&quot;| found in biological membranes. They are synthesized by the addition of an ethanolamine group from CDP-ethanolamine to |FRAME: Diacylglycerides diglycerides|. Phosphatidylethanolamines are found in all living cells, composing 25% of all phospholipids.</Comment>
